cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Cite this software by its title and recorded release or commit. The collective
  author entry is a descriptive project credit, not a verified institutional
  affiliation. Maintainers should replace it with verified contributor metadata
  before an archival release. Also cite the original PCC and BioClaim papers
  below when using the supplied data or inherited split. Software citation does
  not replace data attribution or transfer their licenses.
title: "MASHeart: Reproducible Biomedical Stance Classification and Source-Checked Multi-Agent Review"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
authors:
  - name: MASHeart contributors
abstract: >-
  A standalone educational research workflow for question-conditioned biomedical
  stance classification. It includes source-group data audits, a combined
  word/character TF-IDF Logistic Regression baseline, a T4 QLoRA experiment,
  Analyst-Reviewer-Verifier inference, structural source quotation checks,
  failure-aware evaluation, and an English step-by-step Colab notebook.
keywords:
  - biomedical natural language processing
  - stance classification
  - multi-agent systems
  - QLoRA
  - reproducible research
